--TEST--
`instanceof` is not a Novis operator: `E0253` refuses it where it is written and names `is` — `rule:types/one-type-test`, `rule:types/type-test`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `is` is the one type test (`rule:types/one-type-test`). A written class
// becomes `$x is Animal`, and a class held in a variable becomes `$x is $cls`.
// The refused word does not compile, so a program never changes meaning
// silently over it. The error names the rewrite, and this case pins where it
// points.
class Animal {}

mixed $pet = new Animal();
echo $pet instanceof Animal, "\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0253]: `instanceof` is not a Novis operator; the type test is `is`
   --> %s:10:11
   |
10 | echo $pet instanceof Animal, "\n";
   |           ^^^^^^^^^^ no operator is spelled this way
   = help: write `$x is Request`; a class reference on the right is `$x is $cls` (`rule:types/type-test`)

error: aborting due to 1 error
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
